  "action": "Analyzed Netra Runtime fit for the user's PubMed RAG project. Corrected prior conclusion: RAG has mostly-FRESH input (different retrieved chunks per query, ~10% cache hit), unlike the user's agent loops (90% cache). Modeled per 1,000 queries at 3.5k in / 400 out: Netra .85, OG DeepSeek peak .43, OG off-peak .71. Netra 41% cheaper than OG peak, which matters because Indonesian WIB working hours map almost entirely to OG peak. In high-cache regime OG still wins by 29%. Found blocker: Netra catalog has only 2 chat models, NO embedding model - so Netra covers generation but retrieval/embeddings needs a separate provider (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small or local BGE). Also noted Netra's own comparison tables show Baseten (.13 in on V4 Flash) and CoreWeave (.20/.03/.65) are cheaper on several axes - Netra is not the cheapest reseller, just flat-priced with Indonesian Doku payments."
